    {
        "content": "<p>macovedj opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14455\">PR #14455</a> from <code>macovedj:winch-typed-select-stack-maps</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Winch records a <code>select</code> result using the second operand’s internal type, even for a typed <code>select</code> with a declared result type. In #14451, that operand is <code>ref.null extern</code>, which Winch represents internally as <code>I32</code>. When the condition chooses the live <code>externref</code> from the first operand, the value is correct, but Winch still records the result as <code>I32</code>. The next call’s stack map then omits the live reference, so a collector can lose it.</p>\n<p>This PR records a typed <code>select</code> result using its declared type and adds x86-64 and AArch64 stack-map tests, plus runtime tests for all collectors.</p>\n<p>Fixes #14451.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 628147803,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790788263
